PDF417, GS1 DataBar and Composite immutable symbol facts

The PDF417 cluster codeword patterns, MicroPDF417 layout/initial RAP facts,
and side/centre RAP patterns in src/pdf417/tables.rs are transcribed from
backend/pdf417_tabs.h in Zint commit
4896136bdbebb1a0908a5cc419513efa5bf4bf70 (Zint 2.15.0):
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zint/zint/4896136bdbebb1a0908a5cc419513efa5bf4bf70/backend/pdf417_tabs.h

Only immutable data constants are transferred. Barry's localization, correction
and compaction algorithms are implemented by Barry; no Zint executable or
encoder algorithm is a runtime dependency. Barry restores the omitted trailing
zero module in the writer's sixteen-bit codeword representation.

DataBar width groups, finders, check patterns and Expanded finder sequences
in src/databar/ use ISO/IEC 24724 facts cross-checked against backend/rss.h
at the same Zint commit. CC-A and CC-B layout/RAP witnesses use backend/composite.h
and backend/pdf417_tabs.h from that commit. General-purpose encodation
character assignments are cross-checked against backend/general_field.c.
No restricted BSI implementation routines are included.

ISO/IEC 24723 symbol-separator bit assignments are cross-checked against the
official GS1 Barcode Engine (GS1 AISBL, Apache-2.0), src/c-lib/cc.c at commit
289c8995f001109d0d62e76454f5b1f361dcffae:
https://github.com/gs1/gs1-barcode-engine/blob/289c8995f001109d0d62e76454f5b1f361dcffae/src/c-lib/cc.c
Only wire facts are used; no GS1 engine code or runtime is included.

